@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy";
    Layout = "_Layout";
}

<div class="container-fluid px-0">
    <div class="page-section">
        <div class="mb-4">
            <h1 class="h3 fw-semibold mb-2">Privacy</h1>
            <p class="text-muted mb-0">At ServiceHub IT, we respect the privacy of our clients, technicians, and administrators.</p>
        </div>

        <p>This system may process information required to provide IT support services, including user account details, ticket information, device information, comments, attachments, and service-related records.</p>

        <h2 class="h5 fw-semibold mt-4">How Information Is Used</h2>
        <p>Information collected through the system may be used to:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Manage IT support tickets and service requests.</li>
            <li>Assign tickets to technicians.</li>
            <li>Communicate updates regarding support requests.</li>
            <li>Track ticket progress and resolutions.</li>
            <li>Maintain service and asset records.</li>
            <li>Improve the operation and reliability of the system.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="h5 fw-semibold mt-4">Access to Information</h2>
        <p>Access to information is controlled according to the user's role. Administrators, technicians, and clients have different levels of access based on their responsibilities within the system.</p>
        <p>Users should not attempt to access, modify, or share information that they are not authorized to access.</p>

        <h2 class="h5 fw-semibold mt-4">Data Security</h2>
        <p>The system applies authentication and role-based access controls to help protect information from unauthorized access.</p>

        <h2 class="h5 fw-semibold mt-4">Future Compliance</h2>
        <p>Additional privacy, data-retention, and compliance requirements may be documented here as the system and its organisational requirements develop.</p>

        <p class="mt-4">For questions regarding privacy or information handled by the system, please contact the system administrator.</p>
    </div>
</div>
